19 which was merged before we finished [debating](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107619#discussion_r2152153248) the name of this enum :-)\r\n\r\nI'm not a fan of the existing name for a few reasons:\r\n\r\n1. It uses a lower-case `r` in `OpenXr`, which we don't use anywhere else (except in the C# version of some things that are called `OpenXR*` on the C++ and GDScript side)\r\n2. It's redundant - we don't need to say \"OpenXR\" again, because this is part of `OpenXRInterface`\r\n3. It's inconsistent with the rest of the enums on `OpenXRInterface`, some of which also mirror enums from the OpenXR API (for example, `OpenXRInterface.HandTrackedSource`), but none of the other enums include the  `OpenXR*` prefix\r\n\r\nPerhaps if we started with this convention originally it could make sense, but adding this now doesn't fit in with what we already have","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"